From: PTPT52.AI <ptpt52@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 22:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: fix QDMA TX completion queue marker and visibility

The completion queue is initialized to 0xffffffff, but the consumer
tests and recycles entries using 0x000000ff. The latter can also be a
valid completion for descriptor 255 on ring zero.

Use U32_MAX consistently when reading and recycling entries. The
vendor qdma_bmgr.c also retries when an announced completion is still
0xffffffff: the status can become visible before the queue data.
Use bounded rereads with READ_ONCE and a DMA read barrier; leave an
unpublished entry unconsumed.

This independently identifiable completion-handling defect does not
explain the observed board TX stall, where no completions arrive.

Signed-off-by: PTPT52.AI <ptpt52@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -21,6 +21,9 @@
 #include "airoha_regs.h"
 #include "airoha_eth.h"
 
+#define AIROHA_QDMA_IRQ_ENTRY_INVALID	U32_MAX
+#define AIROHA_QDMA_IRQ_ENTRY_RETRIES	16
+
 u32 airoha_rr(void __iomem *base, u32 offset)
 {
 	return readl(base + offset);
@@ -1222,17 +1225,27 @@ static int airoha_qdma_tx_napi_poll(stru
 	irq_queued = FIELD_GET(IRQ_ENTRY_LEN_MASK, status);
 
 	while (irq_queued > 0 && done < budget) {
-		u32 qid, val = irq_q->q[head];
 		struct airoha_qdma_desc *desc;
 		struct airoha_queue_entry *e;
 		struct airoha_queue *q;
 		u32 index, desc_ctrl;
 		struct sk_buff *skb;
+		u32 qid, val;
+		int retry;
 
-		if (val == 0xff)
+		for (retry = 0; retry < AIROHA_QDMA_IRQ_ENTRY_RETRIES;
+		     retry++) {
+			dma_rmb();
+			val = READ_ONCE(irq_q->q[head]);
+			if (val != AIROHA_QDMA_IRQ_ENTRY_INVALID)
+				break;
+			cpu_relax();
+		}
+		if (val == AIROHA_QDMA_IRQ_ENTRY_INVALID)
 			break;
 
-		irq_q->q[head] = 0xff; /* mark as done */
+		/* Mark the entry free before advancing the hardware queue. */
+		WRITE_ONCE(irq_q->q[head], AIROHA_QDMA_IRQ_ENTRY_INVALID);
 		head = (head + 1) % irq_q->size;
 		irq_queued--;
 		done++;
